  "description": "The Haro SloRide 24\" is our trifecta tribute model to aerial pioneers Brian Blyther, Mike Dominguez and Xavier Mendez. The SloRide has a full 6061 lightweight alloy frame, paired with a full chromoly fork with a custom fade paint scheme and graphics. In the control room, we have 4130 chromoly Haro Freestyler bars with a Haro Baseline 48mm reach stem. Sealed bearings throughout, with double-wall alloy rims mounted with Kenda Kranium tires. A padded, railed seat and custom SloRide are all part of the package. Ready to roll out.\n6061-T6 heat-treated alloy frame w/integrated head tube, mid BB shell & V-brake mounts\n1 1/8\" threadless full chromoly fork w/internally threaded steerer tube & tapered legs\nHaro Baseline 3-pc chromoly 8 Spline 175mm - 39t Steel Chainring\nPoly Platform, chromoly 9/16\" Axle\nHaro freestyler 7\" rise bars\n36h double-wall rims\nHaro SloRide railed seat\nHaro SloRide pad set\nHaro Team grips",
